; The other direction of the same group: zero alternatives present. This is
; what separates `exactly-one` from `at-most-one` — the schema is otherwise
; identical to `exclusive-multi-key-at-most-one`'s, and under that
; cardinality `(route)` would be accepted.
;
; It is also the case that shows the group carries requiredness the keys
; cannot: all three keys are `:optional true`, so no `missing_required_key`
; fires and `(route)` would be silently accepted without the group check.
(plugin :name routes :version "1.0.0"
  (form :name route
    (key :name from :type symbol :optional true)
    (key :name to :type symbol :optional true)
    (key :name at :type symbol :optional true)
    (exclusive-group :cardinality exactly-one
      (alt :keys [from to])
      (alt :keys [at]))))

(route)
